title: Redis Unauthenticated Config Abuse
id: 6b4c9d30-e5dd-4a2a-9844-f84f135cce72
status: experimental
description: Detects abuse of an unauthenticated Redis instance to write arbitrary files (CONFIG SET dir/dbfilename followed by SAVE), a technique to drop web shells, SSH keys, or cron jobs for code execution.
author: Alaris Global
references:
  - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1190/
logsource:
  category: application
  product: redis
detection:
  selection:
    command|contains:
      - 'CONFIG SET dir'
      - 'CONFIG SET dbfilename'
      - 'SLAVEOF'
      - 'MODULE LOAD'
  condition: selection
fields:
  - query_text
  - user_name
  - client_ip
falsepositives:
  - Legitimate Redis administration
level: high
tags:
  - attack.initial_access
  - attack.t1190
